<item>
            <title>[LU-20816] osd-ldiskfs: faked read unlocks a cached DIO folio</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20816</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A read faked with OBD_FAIL_OST_FAKE_RW (0x238) marks its folio&lt;br/&gt;
uptodate, so osd_read_prep() takes the cache-hit branch and unlocks&lt;br/&gt;
the folio.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The per-thread DIO folios are locked when allocated and stay locked&lt;br/&gt;
for as long as the thread caches them; osd_get_folio() reuses them&lt;br/&gt;
without locking again.  Unlocking one in that branch leaves it&lt;br/&gt;
unlocked for its next use, and the next user asserts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  ASSERTION( folio_test_locked(folio) ) failed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Three sites can hit it, all in master:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  osd_write_commit()      lustre/osd-ldiskfs/osd_io.c:1523, 1563&lt;br/&gt;
  osd_read_prep()         lustre/osd-ldiskfs/osd_io.c:1652&lt;br/&gt;
  osd_key_fini()          lustre/osd-ldiskfs/osd_handler.c:8290&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;so a real write or a cache-miss read reusing the folio LBUGs, and&lt;br/&gt;
failing that, the OST LBUGs on unmount when the thread key is torn&lt;br/&gt;
down.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduced on a single node OST with fail_loc=0x238 set and direct&lt;br/&gt;
I/O reads and writes running against it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A real read cannot reach the cache-hit branch holding a DIO folio,&lt;br/&gt;
since osd_get_folio() clears uptodate on each reuse, and page cache&lt;br/&gt;
folios never carry private_2.  Only the faked read gets there.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
